---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SOCIAL } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Maxwell O. Chibuogwu, PhD — postdoctoral fellow at USDA Agricultural Research Service, plant pathologist, and builder of AI tools for African agriculture."
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <!-- ============================================================
         HEADER
         ============================================================ -->
    <header class="about-header">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow reveal">About</p>
        <h1 class="reveal reveal-delay-1">
          A plant pathologist with a problem he can't put down.
        </h1>
        <p class="lede reveal reveal-delay-2">
          Maxwell O. Chibuogwu, PhD. Postdoctoral fellow at the USDA Agricultural
          Research Service, alumnus of UW–Madison, the University of Arizona,
          and the University of Benin — and increasingly, a builder of the
          tools African agriculture has been waiting for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Hero photo -->
    <div class="about-hero-photo reveal reveal-delay-3">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <figure class="hero-fig">
          <img
            src="/images/grad-uw2024.jpg"
            alt="Maxwell O. Chibuogwu in doctoral regalia in front of UW-Madison 2024 sculpture"
            width="1400"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>PhD graduation, University of Wisconsin–Madison, May 2024.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============================================================
         BIO — THE SCIENTIST
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container-narrow prose-editorial">
        <h2>The science came first.</h2>
        <p class="drop-cap">
          I'm a plant pathologist by training. My doctoral work at the
          University of Wisconsin–Madison focused on the integrated management
          of <em>Gibberella</em> diseases and the toxin <em>deoxynivalenol</em>
          (DON) — a mycotoxin produced by <em>Fusarium graminearum</em> that
          accumulates in silage corn and threatens dairy supply chains across
          North America. I defended my dissertation in August 2024 with a
          3.94 GPA and a stack of publications I'm still proud of.
        </p>

        <figure class="inline-fig inline-fig-right">
          <img
            src="/images/grad-dock.jpg"
            alt="Maxwell Chibuogwu in doctoral regalia"
            width="500"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>Bascom Hill, Madison. May 2024 Graduation.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Today I'm an ORISE postdoctoral fellow at the
          <a
            href="https://www.ars.usda.gov/midwest-area/madison-wi/dairy-forage-research-center/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">USDA Dairy Forage Research Center</a>,
          where I lead research on disease and toxin management in dairy
          forages. The work spans field trials, whole-genome sequencing of
          <em>Fusarium</em> species using Oxford Nanopore platforms, fungicide
          resistance evolution under climate change, and predictive modeling
          for mycotoxin detection in silage fields. I am also collaborating
          with industry partners to evaluate postbiotic additives on silage
          fermentation.
        </p>

        <p>
          Before all of that, I trained in molecular plant virology at the
          University of Arizona, working with the Brown Lab on the palo verde
          witches' broom virus — an emaravirus transmitted by eriophyid mites
          across the Sonoran Desert. And before <em>that</em>, my undergraduate
          work at the University of Benin — graduated <em>summa cum laude</em>
          in Plant Biology and Biotechnology — gave me my first taste of
          tissue culture, DNA extraction, and the long, patient art of
          experimental design.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         BIO — THE PIVOT
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="section section-tinted">
      <div class="container-narrow prose-editorial">
        <h2>The pivot — or maybe just the next layer.</h2>
        <p>
          Science taught me what I now believe is the most underrated skill in
          African development: the ability to rigorously distinguish between
          what is true, what is plausible, and what is wishful. Six years of
          field plots and gel electrophoresis builds a particular kind of
          intellectual stamina — one that doesn't tolerate hand-waving when
          the stakes are real.
        </p>

        <p>
          And the stakes <em>are</em> real. While I was learning to model
          fungal pathogens, the
          <a href="https://nimet.gov.ng/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Nigerian Meteorological Agency</a> was — and still is —
          publishing weather bulletins as static PDFs of low-resolution icons,
          pushed out to a country whose smallholder farmers carry nearly all
          the climate risk and almost none of the climate data. That gap, and
          a hundred others like it, is what I've decided I cannot ignore.
        </p>

        <p>
          So I'm building. Vibe-coding, agentic AI, weather APIs, satellite
          imagery, civic dashboards — the whole modern developer stack pointed
          at the boring, unglamorous, deeply consequential infrastructure
          questions African governments have failed to solve. The first product
          is a weather application for Nigerian agricultural cities, comparable
          in quality to what a Wisconsin farmer takes for granted. The
          long-term ambition includes owned satellite data. I'm under no
          illusions about how hard any of this is. I've also spent enough time
          in research to know that hard isn't the same as impossible.
        </p>

        <p>
          This site is where I'll write all of it down — the science, the
          building, and the thinking in between.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         AT A GLANCE
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2 class="glance-title">At a glance.</h2>

        <dl class="glance-list">
          <div>
            <dt>Now</dt>
            <dd>
              ORISE Postdoctoral Fellow, USDA Agricultural Research Service —
              Dairy Forage Research Center, Madison, WI.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Doctorate</dt>
            <dd>
              <div class="edu-entry">
                <img src="/images/logos/uw-madison.png" alt="University of Wisconsin–Madison crest" class="edu-logo" />
                <div>
                  <strong>University of Wisconsin–Madison</strong><br/>
                  PhD, Plant Pathology (3.94 / 4.0) · 2018–2024<br/>
                  Dissertation on integrated management of <em>Gibberella</em> diseases
                  and DON in silage corn.
                  Major advisor: <a href="https://badgercropdoc.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Damon L. Smith</a>.
                </div>
              </div>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Earlier training</dt>
            <dd>
              <div class="edu-entry">
                <img src="/images/logos/u-arizona.svg" alt="University of Arizona" class="edu-logo" />
                <div>
                  <strong>University of Arizona</strong><br/>
                  Graduate studies in molecular plant pathology &amp; plant virology · 2016–2018<br/>
                  Brown Lab — palo verde witches' broom emaravirus and eriophyid mite vectors.
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="edu-entry" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
                <img src="/images/logos/uniben.png" alt="University of Benin" class="edu-logo" />
                <div>
                  <strong>University of Benin</strong><br/>
                  BSc <em>(First Class) or summa cum laude</em>, Plant Biology &amp; Biotechnology · 2010–2015
                </div>
              </div>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Fields</dt>
            <dd>
              Field crop pathology · mycotoxin management · molecular
              virology · whole-genome sequencing · bioinformatics · predictive
              modeling · AI-assisted software development.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Building</dt>
            <dd>
              <a href="/projects">Civic and agricultural tech for African
              markets</a>, beginning with weather products for Nigerian
              farmers. Brand: <em>RethinkNaija</em> (forthcoming).
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div class="glance-awards">
            <dt>Recognized for</dt>
            <dd>
              <p>1st place, MANRRS Region V Business Pitch Contest 2023 —
              a $12,000 scholarship to the Draper University Summer Entrepreneurship
              Bootcamp in Silicon Valley, where Team Lightning went on to win the
              programme-wide competition out of ~10 teams.
              Also: American Farm Bureau Federation Fellowship (2023) ·
              I.E. Melhus Graduate Symposium Award (2023) · Best Lightning Talk,
              12th Plant Sciences Symposium (2022) · Multiple departmental
              fellowships and travel grants.</p>
              <div class="award-photos award-photos-4">
                <figure>
                  <img src="/images/manrrs-award.jpg" alt="Receiving MANRRS Region V pitch contest award" loading="lazy" />
                  <figcaption>MANRRS Region V Pitch Contest — 1st place, 2023</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <img src="/images/manrrs-national.jpg" alt="MANRRS national conference award" loading="lazy" />
                  <figcaption>MANRRS national conference award</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <img src="/images/draper-capes.jpg" alt="Team Lightning at Draper University, Silicon Valley — Maxwell's cape reads 'Captain Future'" loading="lazy" />
                  <figcaption>Draper University, Silicon Valley — Team Lightning. Cape: <em>Captain Future</em>.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <img src="/images/draper-team.jpg" alt="Team Lightning winning the Draper University competition" loading="lazy" />
                  <figcaption>Team Lightning — 1st place, Draper University Bootcamp 2023</figcaption>
                </figure>
              </div>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Affiliations</dt>
            <dd>
              American Phytopathological Society (APS) · Mycological Society of
              America (MSA) · American Society for Microbiology (ASM) ·
              Minorities in Agriculture, Natural Resources and Related Sciences
              (MANRRS).
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Based in</dt>
            <dd>Madison, Wisconsin.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         IN THE PRESS
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="section section-tinted">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2 class="glance-title">In the press.</h2>
        <ul class="press-list">
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://news.cals.wisc.edu/2024/04/19/spring-2024-grad-maxwell-chibuogwu/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              <span class="press-source">UW–Madison CALS News</span>
              <span class="press-title">Spring 2024 grad: Maxwell Chibuogwu studies crop pathogens, earns PhD to support agriculture in African nations</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://grow.cals.wisc.edu/departments/features/emissaries-of-science"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              <span class="press-source">CALS Grow Magazine</span>
              <span class="press-title">Emissaries of Science — cover feature on the WEMP program</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://hoards.com/article-33733-silage-mycotoxins-can-intensify-in-silos.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              <span class="press-source">Hoard's Dairyman</span>
              <span class="press-title">Silage mycotoxins can intensify in silos</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://international.wisc.edu/phd-student-supporting-international-students-through-involvement-and-growing-uw-madisons-web/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              <span class="press-source">UW–Madison International Division</span>
              <span class="press-title">PhD student supporting international students through involvement</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://wiagribusiness.org/2023-classic-speakers/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              <span class="press-source">Wisconsin Agribusiness Classic</span>
              <span class="press-title">Speaker, 2023 Agribusiness Classic</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.fb.org/news-release/afbf-fellowships-bring-manrrs-student-members-to-leadership-conference"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              <span class="press-source">American Farm Bureau Federation</span>
              <span class="press-title">AFBF Fellowships bring MANRRS student members to leadership conference</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://ecals.cals.wisc.edu/2024/04/24/uw-manrrs-students-thrive-at-national-conference/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              <span class="press-source">eCALS</span>
              <span class="press-title">UW MANRRS students thrive at national conference</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         CONTACT
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <div class="contact-card">
          <h2>Get in touch.</h2>
          <p>
            The fastest channel is LinkedIn. I'm especially keen to hear from
            researchers, developers, and funders working at the intersection
            of agriculture, AI, and African development.
          </p>
          <div class="contact-links">
            <a href={SOCIAL.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">
              LinkedIn
            </a>
            <a href="/blog" class="btn-ghost">Read the blog</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5rem) 2rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vh, 4rem);
  }

  .section-tinted {
    background-color: var(--surface);
  }

  .prose-editorial h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .glance-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     AT A GLANCE list
     ============================================================ */
  .glance-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .glance-list > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .glance-list > div:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .glance-list dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .glance-list dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     PRESS
     ============================================================ */
  .press-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .press-list li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .press-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .press-list a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 14rem 1fr auto;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text);
    transition: padding 0.2s ease;
  }

  .press-list a:hover {
    padding-left: 0.5rem;
  }

  .press-list a::after {
    content: '↗';
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    align-self: center;
    opacity: 0.5;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .press-list a:hover::after {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translate(2px, -2px);
  }

  .press-source {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    align-self: center;
  }

  .press-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     CONTACT CARD
     ============================================================ */
  .contact-card {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse 100% 80% at 50% 0%,
      var(--accent-soft),
      transparent 70%
    );
  }

  .contact-card h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .contact-card p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 50ch;
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .btn-primary,
  .btn-ghost {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--color-cream-50);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
  }

  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .btn-primary {
    color: var(--color-forest-900);
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background-color: var(--accent-hover);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .btn-ghost {
    color: var(--text);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background-color: transparent;
  }

  .btn-ghost:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     RESPONSIVE
     ============================================================ */
  /* ============================================================
     HERO PHOTO
     ============================================================ */
  .about-hero-photo {
    margin-block: 2rem 0;
  }

  .hero-fig {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    max-height: 540px;
  }

  .hero-fig img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 20%;
    display: block;
  }

  .hero-fig figcaption {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    font-style: italic;
    background-color: var(--surface);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     INLINE FLOATED FIGURE
     ============================================================ */
  .inline-fig {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .inline-fig img {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .inline-fig figcaption {
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    font-style: italic;
    background-color: var(--surface);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .inline-fig-right {
    float: right;
    width: 38%;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     EDUCATION ENTRIES WITH LOGOS
     ============================================================ */
  .edu-entry {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .edu-logo {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    object-fit: contain;
    object-position: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .edu-logo-svg {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: block;
    width: 120px;
  }

  .edu-logo-svg svg {
    width: 120px;
    height: 36px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: block;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     AWARD PHOTOS GRID
     ============================================================ */
  .award-photos {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .award-photos-4 {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  }

  .award-photos figure {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .award-photos img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center top;
    display: block;
  }

  .award-photos figcaption {
    padding: 0.5rem 0.625rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    font-style: italic;
    background-color: var(--surface);
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     RESPONSIVE
     ============================================================ */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .glance-list > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .press-list a {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .press-source {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
    .inline-fig-right {
      float: none;
      width: 100%;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    .award-photos {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .award-photos-4 {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .edu-entry {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.625rem;
    }

    .edu-logo-svg {
      width: 100px;
    }

    .edu-logo-svg svg {
      width: 100px;
      height: 30px;
    }
  }
</style>
